skills/
# ...but first-party Claude Code skills are repo tooling and belong in version control.
# (.claude/ itself is already tracked — settings.json, hooks/.) Git will not descend into
# an excluded directory, so .claude/skills/ must be re-included before a child negation
# can take effect. Installed/third-party skills stay ignored; add one negation per skill
# we author ourselves.
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/delegate/
instructions/
agents/
go-to-market-docs/
brand-identity-pharma-apps/
brand-identity/

# Real pharmacy data with sensitive information
backend/src/tests/fixtures/real-pharmacy-products.csv
supplier-doc-examples/*
!supplier-doc-examples/sample_100_ipa_price_brands.xlsx

